<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Harihara II</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. 1377–1404</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harihara">Harihara</a> II was emperor of Vijayanagara of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sangama-dynasty">Sangama dynasty</a> from 1377 to 1404, the son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bukka-raya-i">Bukka I</a>. He consolidated the empire's hold on southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, extending its control along the west coast and over the Tamil lands, and fought the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bahmani-sultanate">Bahmani Sultanate</a> for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/raichur-doab">Raichur Doab</a>. He was the first ruler of the dynasty to take imperial titles such as Rajadhiraja.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/harihara-ii.jpg" alt="Harihara II" width="320" height="177" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Harihara_II_Coin.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
